### ============================================
### AREAS — REST Client
### ============================================
### Primero haz login para obtener el token.
### POST http://localhost:8000/api/auth/login
### Content-Type: application/json
###
### {"user": "1193377218", "pass": "1193377218"}
### ============================================

### ============================================
### LISTADO
### ============================================

### 1. OBTENER todas las áreas
GET http://localhost:8000/api/areas

### ============================================
### FILTRO
### ============================================

### 2. FILTRAR áreas por nombre
GET http://localhost:8000/api/areas/filtro?filtro=S40

### 3. FILTRAR áreas — sin coincidencias (debe retornar data vacío)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/areas/filtro?filtro=areainexistentexyz

### ============================================
### ACTUALIZAR
### ============================================

### 4. ACTUALIZAR área — exitoso
PUT http://localhost:8000/api/areas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id": 1,
    "nombre": "S40 (1B)",
    "user_log": 1,
    "activo": 1
}

### 5. ACTUALIZAR área — ID inexistente (debe fallar)
PUT http://localhost:8000/api/areas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id": 99999,
    "nombre": "Área fantasma",
    "user_log": 1,
    "activo": 1
}

### ============================================
### ESTADO
### ============================================

### 6. CAMBIAR estado de áreas — desactivar
POST http://localhost:8000/api/areas/estado
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "ids": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
    "estado": 0
}

### 7. CAMBIAR estado de áreas — reactivar
POST http://localhost:8000/api/areas/estado
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "ids": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
    "estado": 1
}

### ============================================
### ASIGNAR
### ============================================

### 8. ASIGNAR área a un usuario (actualiza inventario de esa área)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/areas/asignar
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_user": 3123,
    "id_area": 104
}

### 9. ASIGNAR área — sin inventario en el área (debe fallar)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/areas/asignar
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_user": 3123,
    "id_area": 99999
}
